(3. The conventional fix, and why it needs adapting) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 56 702.00 Tm
( ) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 687.00 Tm
(Corporations facing this exact problem use a forward contract: an) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 672.00 Tm
(agreement to exchange currency at an agreed rate on a future date. It) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 657.00 Tm
(removes the guesswork, at the cost of giving up any upside if the rate) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 642.00 Tm
(moves in your favour.) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 619.00 Tm
( ) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 600.00 Tm
(In traditional Islamic finance, a standard forward can be problematic:) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 585.00 Tm
(it fixes an exchange today for currency that is only actually delivered) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 570.00 Tm
(later, without either side taking possession at the time of the) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 555.00 Tm
(agreement. That structure is part of what scholars have raised concerns) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 540.00 Tm
(about in currency forwards generally.) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 515.00 Tm
( ) Tj
/F2 13 Tf
1 0 0 1 56 494.00 Tm
(4. Wa'ad: the Shariah-compliant alignment) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 56 475.00 Tm
( ) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 460.00 Tm
(Modern Islamic finance addresses this with Wa'ad - a binding unilateral) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 445.00 Tm
(promise. Under a Wa'ad structure:) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 426.00 Tm
( ) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 411.00 Tm
(- The agency \(or the provider\) makes a binding promise today to) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 396.00 Tm
(  exchange currency at a specific rate on a specific future date.) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 381.00 Tm
(- No exchange of money happens at the time of the promise.) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 366.00 Tm
(- The actual transaction and exchange only occur on the maturity date) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 351.00 Tm
(  itself, when both sides genuinely deliver what was promised.) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 328.00 Tm
( ) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 309.00 Tm
(The economics are the same as a forward - your rate is locked - but the) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 294.00 Tm
(structure \(a promise, executed later, rather than a same-day exchange) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 279.00 Tm
(of undelivered currency\) is what modern Islamic corporate banking desks) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 264.00 Tm
(use to offer this while respecting Islamic financial frameworks.) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 241.00 Tm
( ) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 222.00 Tm
(Important: most conventional fintech providers \(OFX included\) offer the) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 207.00 Tm
(same underlying economic structure as a Wa'ad, but typically without a) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 192.00 Tm
(formal Shariah certification board attached to it. If certification) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 177.00 Tm
(matters to your agency, ask for it explicitly - see the checklist.) Tj
